---
import ContentLayout from "../../../../layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
---
<ContentLayout title="Aurora OS Add-ons" description="A manually curated, static preview of ideas for the future Aurora OS add-on catalogue." eyebrow="AURORA OS / ADD-ONS" heading="Extend the system." lead="A curated shortlist of add-on ideas for Aurora OS. Nothing here is downloadable or endorsed as compatible yet: each entry is a direction to explore, selected and maintained manually.">
  <section class="section shell product-catalogue">
    <div class="catalogue-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">STATIC CURATION / NO SUBMISSIONS</p>
      <h2>A catalogue with a human hand behind it.</h2>
      <p class="content-copy">Aurora add-ons will be selected by the project maintainer. There are no publisher accounts, community submissions, automatic rankings or package downloads. Ideas stay ideas until an actual project is selected, reviewed and verified.</p>
      <p class="catalogue-status"><span class="status-dot"></span> PLANNED — CURATED DIRECTORY</p>
    </div>

    <section class="catalogue-group" aria-labelledby="os-must-have">
      <div class="catalogue-heading"><p class="eyebrow">01 / FOUNDATION</p><h2 id="os-must-have">Must-have</h2><p>Core utilities that could make a new operating-system environment practical to use and maintain.</p></div>
      <div class="catalogue-grid">
        <article class="catalogue-card"><span>IDEA / SYSTEM</span><h3>System Monitor</h3><p>Inspect CPU, memory, storage and running services through a clear, resource-conscious interface.</p></article>
        <article class="catalogue-card"><span>IDEA / DATA</span><h3>Backup &amp; Snapshots</h3><p>Create, inspect and restore user-data backups, with transparent retention and recovery behaviour.</p></article>
        <article class="catalogue-card"><span>IDEA / FILES</span><h3>Archive Manager</h3><p>Browse and extract common archive formats while making paths and file operations explicit.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="catalogue-group" aria-labelledby="os-trending">
      <div class="catalogue-heading"><p class="eyebrow">02 / EDITORIAL PICKS</p><h2 id="os-trending">Trending ideas</h2><p>Topics currently on the curator's radar. This is not a popularity chart, usage statistic or automated trend feed.</p></div>
      <div class="catalogue-grid">
        <article class="catalogue-card"><span>IDEA / DIAGNOSTICS</span><h3>Hardware &amp; Health Inspector</h3><p>A focused view of detected hardware, device health signals and diagnostic information.</p></article>
        <article class="catalogue-card"><span>IDEA / WORKFLOW</span><h3>Quick Launcher</h3><p>Search applications, settings and common actions from one keyboard-driven interface.</p></article>
        <article class="catalogue-card"><span>IDEA / NETWORK</span><h3>Network Diagnostics</h3><p>Understand connectivity, active interfaces and basic network troubleshooting information.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="catalogue-group" aria-labelledby="os-developer">
      <div class="catalogue-heading"><p class="eyebrow">03 / TECHNICAL</p><h2 id="os-developer">Developer &amp; power-user tools</h2><p>Potential tools for inspecting and understanding the system without weakening its security boundaries.</p></div>
      <div class="catalogue-grid">
        <article class="catalogue-card"><span>IDEA / LOGGING</span><h3>Log Explorer</h3><p>Filter system logs and diagnostics with useful context and export controls.</p></article>
        <article class="catalogue-card"><span>IDEA / PACKAGES</span><h3>Package Inspector</h3><p>Review package metadata, origin, integrity information and declared permissions before installation.</p></article>
        <article class="catalogue-card"><span>IDEA / CUSTOMIZATION</span><h3>Desktop Themes</h3><p>Apply coherent visual themes with predictable settings and accessible contrast.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <p class="evidence-note">All entries on this page are proposals only. They do not imply that Aurora OS currently supports add-ons, package installation, or any listed capability.</p>
    <a class="text-link" href="/en/ecosystem/os/">← Back to Aurora OS</a>
  </section>
</ContentLayout>
